  "details": "I'm pretty sure a lot of people are selective mute, medically mute, or deaf, so it would be good to have a preference of what they would like to be used as a chatting feature, whether that be the chat box or actual voice. I know there is already a live caption feature on quest, not sure about PC. , but it would also be very useful if we had a localized chat box with what other players are saying. Of course there might be some legal issues with them being put through a translator box, but they could opt out if they don't want to have their voice put through the local assistance. Another idea is if somebody else speaks a different language, it can be translated by other players putting in input of what the other language is trying to say in a more recognizable manner.",
